<h3>Pre-laminated HDHMR (a separate category)</h3>
<p>Many vendors quote "pre-laminated HDHMR" — boards that come with a thin decorative laminate pre-bonded at the factory. These run roughly 50–80% more expensive than plain HDHMR at the same thickness. Pre-lam saves labour on internal carcass work and looks acceptable for hidden surfaces. For exposed shutters, separate HDHMR + premium laminate gives a better result.</p>
<h3>Real-project pricing context</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>10ft modular kitchen (HDHMR carcass + shutters + laminate):</strong> ₹85,000 – 1.4 lakhs for the materials and finish</li>
  <li><strong>8ft master wardrobe (HDHMR carcass + laminated shutters):</strong> ₹35,000 – 60,000</li>
  <li><strong>Full 3BHK home (HDHMR throughout):</strong> ₹2.8 – 4.5 lakhs in board and finish costs</li>
</ul>
<p>For comparison, switching the same projects to BWP marine plywood adds roughly 25–40% to the board cost. Switching to particle board cuts cost by 35–45% but the furniture won't last more than 4–5 years.</p>
